# Format: one entry per line — `<file relative to frontend/>: <exact phrase
# or substring>  # reason`. The checker (scripts/check-naming.mjs) only
# suppresses a hit when the flagged text node contains this exact phrase, so
# keep phrases specific rather than single words.
#
# Scope (Ruling T19b): the naming rule governs what LotLogic calls its
# passes — UI labels, pass categories, product copy naming a pass type. It
# does NOT govern plain-English or industry nouns describing people or
# occupations (a tow truck driver on patrol, "900,000 residents" as a city
# population figure, a rideshare driver, quoted speech). Entries below are
# either that, or a genuine legal term of art in a legal-adjacent page. If a
# sentence is actually naming a LotLogic pass type, rewrite it to say
# "parking pass" instead of allow-listing it.
#
# NOTE: this guard reads HTML text nodes only. It cannot see
# frontend/policy/*.jpg — the printed-document images rendered from
# charlotte-travel-plaza.src.html. Those must be regenerated by hand
# whenever the .src.html text changes (see task-19-report.md for the
# render command); the guard passing does not mean the JPGs are in sync.

